road node stores reference to the next road form and the prior road form
as well as the id that the road form assigned to it

road follower moves with a speed to the form.next().position, every frame it checks if it can move
towards the targeted position that frame, it does not move if it cannot

# road node

* ref to position
* ref to next
* ref to prev

# road form

* list of nodes
* function next(node_id) -> node, must always return the same thing
* function full() -> bool, returns if the follower can enter the segment
* function entered(node_id) -> ticket, called when a follower enters the segment
* function left(node_id, ticket), called when a follower exits the segment
* function can_move_to(node_id, position, ticket) -> bool, whether the position is available 

# road follower

* ref to entry node
* ref to current form